# Names for the "Network usage (per device)" Grafana dashboard.
# Copy to device-names (gitignored, like docs/hardware.md: it maps the LAN's
# addresses to what they are) and edit; usage_textfile.sh rereads it every
# minute, no restart needed.
#
#   <ip, mac or tailscale label>  <name, may contain spaces>
#
# By MAC suits a phone or laptop on the router's own WiFi, which keeps its
# MAC when DHCP gives it a new IP. Devices behind the TP-Link extender all
# share the extender's MAC (the router cannot reserve IPs for them either),
# so name those by Tailscale, or by IP set manually on the device.
# A device running Tailscale is named by its MagicDNS label (iphone-14) with
# no entry here; list the label to show a nicer name. Order: MAC, Tailscale,
# IP, then the router's hostname, then the IP itself.
192.168.1.124  wol Pi
aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff  Someone's phone
iphone-14  iPhone 14
